The Stan, WebPPL and Psi programs of the bit-blasting paper's artifact
(Garg, Holtzen, Van den Broeck and Millstein, "Bit Blasting Probabilistic
Programs", PLDI 2024), which scripts/samplers/samplers.py runs.

Source: https://github.com/Tractables/Alea.jl, branch hybit, commit
96b69a58 ("simple examples added"), Apache License 2.0.

  baselines/stan, baselines/webppl   hybrid/baselines/{stan,webppl}: only the
                                     .stan, .data.R and .wppl files (the
                                     artifact's compiled models are left out)
  benchmarks/                        hybrid/benchmarks/{or,multimodal,
                                     conjugate_gaussians}: the same files
  psi/                               hybrid/baselines/psi: the .psi programs,
                                     data/ and or/
  psi/cobs/                          ours: altermu2, conjugate_gaussians and
                                     normal_mixture with each
                                     `observe(gauss(m, s) == y)` written as
                                     `cobserve(gauss(m, s), y)`. Psi treats
                                     the first as an observation of an event
                                     of probability zero (it prints a
                                     posterior density 0 and Pr[error] = 1);
                                     the second conditions on the density.
